            %p
              may be obtained from a choice of
              %em dual basis
              to the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\partial_\alpha \delta_0\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msup
                          %mi w
                          %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mi cp
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo }
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi β
                            %mo ∈
                            %msup
                              %mi ℕ
                              %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi β
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    w^\beta \in C^\infty_{cp}(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\right\}_{ { \beta \in \mathbb{N}^n } \atop { {\vert \beta\vert} \leq \rho } }
            %p such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi w
                        %mi β
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi α
                      %mi β
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %msup
                      %mi w
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi α
                      %mi β
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mtext for
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\langle
                    \\partial_\alpha \delta_0
                    \\,,\,
                    w^\beta
                    \\right\rangle
                    \\;=\;
                    \\delta_\alpha^\beta
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\partial_\alpha w^\beta(0)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\delta_\alpha^\beta
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    \\text{for}\, {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho
                    \\,,
            %p by setting
            #eq:SpaceOfSmoothFunctionsOfGivenVaishingOrderProjector.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi α
                              %mo ∈
                              %msup
                                %mi ℕ
                                %mi n
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi α
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi ρ
                      %msup
                        %mi w
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_\rho
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    id
                    \\;-\;
                    \\left\langle
                    \\underset{
                    {\alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n}
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho }
                    }{\sum}
                    w^\alpha \partial_\alpha \delta_0
                    \\,,\,
                    (-)
                    \\right\rangle
                    \\,,
            %p hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi b
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi b
                    %mo −
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ∈
                            %msup
                              %mi ℕ
                              %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mi w
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_\rho
                    \\;\colon\;
                    b
                    \\mapsto
                    b
                    \-
                    \\underset{
                    {\alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n}
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho }
                    }{\sum}
                    (-1)^{{\vert \alpha\vert}} w^\alpha \partial_\alpha b(0)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Together with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard%27s+lemma"} Hadamard's lemma
              in the form
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ForVanishingOrderRhoHadamardExpansion"} (1)
              this means that every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \mathcal{D}(\mathbb{R}^n)
              is decomposed as
            #eq:ForExtensionOfDistributionsTestFunctionDecomposition.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi id
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi α
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %msup
                                      %mi ℕ
                                      %mi n
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mi α
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mo =
                                    %mi ρ
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi α
                            %msub
                              %mi r
                              %mi α
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi α
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %msup
                                      %mi ℕ
                                      %mi n
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mi α
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mo ≤
                                    %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi α
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %msup
                              %mi w
                              %mi α
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi α
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    b(x)
                    \&amp; =
                    p_\rho(b)(x)
                    \\;+\;
                    (id - p_\rho)(b)(x)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{
                    { \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n }
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha \vert} = \rho + 1 }
                    }{\sum}
                    x^\alpha r_\alpha(x)
                    \\;+\;
                    \\underset{
                    { \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n }
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha \vert} \leq \rho }
                    }{\sum}
                    (-1)^{{\vert \alpha \vert}}
                    w^\alpha \partial_\alpha b(0)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p Now let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    deg(u)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "scaling+degree+of+a+distribution#ScalingDegreeOfDistributionsBasicProperties"} this prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+divergence+of+a+distribution"} degree of divergence
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\alpha u
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert \alpha\vert} = \rho + 1
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi deg
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mi α
                              %mi u
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo −
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo ≤
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    deg\left(
                    x^\alpha u
                    \\right)
                    \&amp; =
                    \\rho - {\vert \alpha \vert}
                    \\leq
                    \-1
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Therefore prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExtensionUniqueNonPositiveDegreeOfDivergence"}
              says that each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^\alpha u
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert \alpha\vert} = \rho + 1
              has a unique extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi α
                        %mi u
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{ x^\alpha u}
              to the origin. Accordingly the composition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \circ p_\rho
              has a unique extension, by
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ForExtensionOfDistributionsTestFunctionDecomposition"} (3)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo ⟨
                              %mover
                                %mi u
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi b
                              %mo ⟩
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mrow
                              %mo ⟨
                              %mover
                                %mi u
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi ρ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⟩
                            %mo +
                            %mrow
                              %mo ⟨
                              %mover
                                %mi u
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mo ,
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi id
                              %mo −
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi ρ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⟩
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi α
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %msup
                                      %mi ℕ
                                      %mi n
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mi α
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mo =
                                    %mi ρ
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ⟨
                                  %mover
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi x
                                        %mi α
                                      %mi u
                                    %mo ^
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %msub
                                    %mi r
                                    %mi α
                                  %mo ⟩
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mtext unique
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo +
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi α
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %msup
                                      %mi ℕ
                                      %mi n
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mi α
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mo ≤
                                    %mi ρ
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                  %mover
                                    %mi u
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %msup
                                    %mi w
                                    %mi α
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mtext choice
                            %mrow
                              %mo ⟨
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi α
                              %msub
                                %mi δ
                                %mn 0
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi b
                              %mo ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\left\langle
                    \\hat u
                    \\,,\,
                    b
                    \\right\rangle
                    \&amp; =
                    \\left\langle
                    \\hat u
                    ,
                    p_\rho(b)
                    \\right\rangle
                    +
                    \\left\langle
                    \\hat u
                    ,
                    (id - p_\rho)(b)
                    \\right\rangle
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{
                    { \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n }
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha \vert} = \rho + 1 }
                    }{\sum}
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{unique}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\left\langle
                    \\widehat{x^\alpha u}
                    \\,,\,
                    r_\alpha
                    \\right\rangle
                    }
                    }
                    \\;+\;
                    \\underset{
                    { \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n }
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho }
                    }{\sum}
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{choice}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\langle
                    \\hat u
                    \\,,\,
                    w^\alpha
                    \\rangle
                    }
                    }
                    \\left\langle
                    \\partial_\alpha \delta_0
                    \\,,\,
                    b
                    \\right\rangle
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              That says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat u
              is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mi u
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi ρ
                          %mo ^
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext unique
                    %mo +
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ∈
                            %msup
                              %mi ℕ
                              %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ρ
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mi α
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat u
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{unique}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\widehat{
                    u \circ p_\rho
                    }
                    }
                    }
                    +
                    \\underset{
                    { \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n  }
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho }
                    }{\sum}
                    c^\alpha
                    \\,
                    \\partial_\alpha \delta_0
            %p
              for a finite number of constants
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^\alpha \in \mathbb{C}
            %p
              Notice that for any extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat u
              the exact value of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^\alpha
              here depends on the arbitrary choice of dual basis
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi w
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{w^\alpha\}
              used for this construction. But the uniqueness of the first summand means that for any two choices of extensions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat u
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\hat u}^\prime
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ∈
                            %msup
                              %mi ℕ
                              %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi α
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\hat u}^\prime - \hat u
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{
                    { \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n  }
                    \\atop
                    { {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho }
                    }{\sum}
                    ( (c')^\alpha - c^\alpha )
                    \\,
                    \\partial_\alpha \delta_0
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the constants
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mi α
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi α
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q^\alpha \coloneqq ( (c')^\alpha - c^\alpha ) \in \mathbb{C}
              are independent of any choices.
            %p
              It remains to see that all these
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat u
              in fact have the same degree of divergence as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "scaling+degree+of+a+distribution#DerivativesOfDeltaDistributionScalingDegree"} this example
              the degree of divergence of the point-supported distributions on the right is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(\partial_\alpha \delta_0) = {\vert \alpha\vert} \leq \rho
            %p Therefore to conclude it is now sufficient to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi u
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi ρ
                        %mo ^
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    deg\left(
                    \\widehat{
                    u \circ p_\rho
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\rho
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is shown in (
              %a{:href => "#BrunettiFredenhagen00"}> Brunetti-Fredenhagen 00, p. 25
              ).
          #WExtensions.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong (“W-extensions”)
            %p
              Since in
              %a{:href => "#BrunettiFredenhagen00"} Brunetti-Fredenhagen 00, (38)
              the projectors
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpaceOfSmoothFunctionsOfGivenVaishingOrderProjector"} (2)
              are denoted “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              ”, the construction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions+of+distributions"} extensions of distributions
              via the proof of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpaceOfPointExtensions"}
              has come to be called “W-extensions” (e.g
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Duetsch18"} Dütsch 18
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#powers_of_feynman_propagators Powers of Feynman propagators
          %p
            Extension of powers of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagators"} Feynman propagators
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            are worked out explicitly in (
            %a{:href => "#Hollands07"}> Hollands 07, section 3.4
            ).
          %h2#references References
          %p The argument for the characterization of the point extension of distributions goes back to
          %ul
            %li#EpsteinGlaser73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Epstein"} Henri Epstein
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Glaser"} Vladimir Glaser
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+role+of+locality+in+perturbation+theory"} The role of locality in perturbation theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=AIHPA_1973__19_3_211_0"} Numdam
          %p
            thereby laying the foundation for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Hoermander14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+H%C3%B6rmander"}> Lars Hörmander
              , theorem 3.2.4 of
              %em The Analysis of Linear Partial Differential Operators I
              (Springer, 1990, 2nd ed.)
          %p A more concise formulation and proof is due to
          %ul
            %li#BrunettiFredenhagen00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Microlocal analysis and interacting quantum field theories: Renormalization on Physical Backgrounds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/9903028"} math-ph/9903028
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Duetsch18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
              , theorem 3.35 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/From+classical+field+theory+to+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} From classical field theory to perturbative quantum field theory
          %p
            Exposition of the application to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Brouder10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Brouder"}> Christian Brouder
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multiplication of distributions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BrouderProductOfDistributions.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The refinement to the point-extension problem for distributions in the solution space of a given system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equations"} differential equations
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BahnsWrochna12
              Dorothea Bahns, Michał Wrochna,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On-shell extension of distributions
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1210.5448"} arXiv:1210.5448
          %p
            Examples and applications to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            are discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Hollands07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Hollands"}> Stefan Hollands
              , sections 3.3 and 3.4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Renormalized Quantum Yang-Mills Fields in Curved Spacetime
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.3340"} arXiv:0705.3340
          %p
            For more on extension of distributions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            see the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative quantum field theory
